> ### Foreword by the Minister of Finance of Uganda
> 
> Dear Colleagues,
> 
> As we navigate an era marked by unprecedented challenges and opportunities, the imperative to confront climate change stands at the forefront of our collective agenda. The economic upheaval resulting from deteriorating environmental conditions is stark and inescapable, with fiscal landscapes across the globe feeling the pressure of its far-reaching implications. 
> 
> This report serves as a critical synthesis of an extensive body of research, highlighting the economic peril we face due to the physical impacts of climate change and articulating a clear economic justification for investing in adaptation measures. Grounded in nearly 300 studies, it offers a comprehensive picture of the evolving climate risks and underscores the pressing need for preemptive, strategic action.
> 
> For Finance Ministries and economic leaders worldwide, this calls for us to pivot from reactionary fiscal measures toward visionary investments in adaptation that promise economic stability and sustainable growth. The fiscal implications are profound—with adaptation investments serving not only to curtail losses but to foster resilience and enhance our economies' productivity and integrity. This proactive approach offers a new paradigm for managing the macroeconomic risks of climate change, integrating adaptation with fiscal policy and strategic national economic planning.
> 
> Moreover, the report highlights a critical opening for collaboration and innovation. By engaging with diverse stakeholders, from governments to the private sector, we can cultivate environments conducive to private investment and ensure the adaptation measures we implement are impactful and widespread. In a world where the interconnectedness of climate impacts knows no borders, it is our responsibility to craft adaptive solutions that are both locally relevant and universally beneficial.
> 
> The path ahead requires bold leadership and a commitment to transformation. This report not only equips us with valuable insights and frameworks but also calls us to action. As Finance Ministers, we have a pivotal role in safeguarding our countries' economic futures; adaptation is not an auxiliary choice but a strategic imperative to secure our nations' prosperity in the face of climate challenges.
> 
> I commend this report to you, trusting it will inform and inspire our efforts to build resilient economies that thrive amidst the changes of our world.
> 
> Sincerely,
> 
> [The Minister of Finance, Uganda]
